    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d837">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1243" xml:id="pg1243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Korea/6–1548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d837-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-15T14:00:00+09:00">July 15, 1948—2 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1296. Reference Embtel 1209, July 2, 2 p. m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d837-f2"/>
                    Foreign Minister<anchor n="3" xml:id="d837-f3"/> has now informed us that China
                    will definitely join the US in any action to recognize a national government of
                    Korea. He suggests that the US and China undertake a joint <hi
                        rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> to secure simultaneous and similar British
                    action. He further suggests that the American Ambassador in Paris be instructed
                    to renew his efforts vis-à-vis French Government.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d837-f4"
                    />
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d837-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d837-f1-content">
                <p>Sent as 253, July 21, 5 p. m., to Seoul.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d837-f2" n="2" xml:id="d837-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d837-f3" n="3" xml:id="d837-f3-content">
                <p>Dr. Wang Shih-chieh.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d837-f4" n="4" xml:id="d837-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 1045, July 17, 5 p. m., to Nanking, the Department expressed
                    appreciation of Chinese support, agreed as to appropriateness of parallel
                    statements by the U.S., United Kingdom, and China, stated it was “most anxious
                    that such joint action be arranged”, and was delaying further approach to France
                    pending a reaction to the circular telegram of July 10, 1 a. m., <ref
                        target="#pg1235">p. 1235</ref>. This telegram was repeated as 2800 to London
                    and as 242 to Seoul.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
